// Hinglish — Roman-script Hindi mixed with English (VOCAB_HINGLISH in grammar.ts).
// In scope for MVP, and the reason the grammar keeps its vocabulary in TABLES
// rather than inline in regexes: adding a language must be data, not code.
//
// ALL TEXT IS FABRICATED. Aliases point at the synthetic runner.mjs fixture.
//
// The shape of this bucket is the finding: a Hinglish CATEGORY word (khana,
// kirana, kiraya, bijli, dawai, kapde, tankhwah) works end-to-end and writes,
// because the trailing-alias heuristic hangs off a matched category. A Hinglish
// VERB (kharcha, bheje, nikala, mila) sets a direction that validator.ts — whose
// vocabulary is English-only — cannot corroborate, so the pipeline asks about
// polarity instead. Asking is safe; the asymmetry is worth knowing about.
